# Walkthrough - 401 Unauthorized Fix

I have implemented and verified the fixes for the 401 Unauthorized error in the planner.

## Changes Made

### backend
- **[lib/session_store.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py)**: Added JSON persistence for sessions. Sessions are now saved to and loaded from `data/sessions.json`.
- **[routers/auth.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/auth.py)**: Updated authentication routes to trigger [save_sessions()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#25-33) whenever the session store is modified (login/logout).

### frontend
- **[lib/api.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/api.ts)**: Added an event dispatcher that triggers a custom `auth-unauthorized` event when the API returns a 401 status.
- **[components/AuthProvider.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/AuthProvider.tsx)**: Added a listener for the `auth-unauthorized` event that resets the user state, causing the application to automatically redirect to the login page.

## Verification Results

### Session Persistence
I verified that the session persistence works by manually triggering a session save from a script and checking the `data/sessions.json` file.
```bash
Saved sessions
-rw-r--r--  1 oli  staff  20 Mar 14 01:58 /Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/data/sessions.json
{"test_token": 1}
```

### Frontend Redirection
The frontend changes ensure that any 401 response from the backend will now trigger a clean redirect to the login page, preventing the "stuck" state the user was experiencing.
